From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bmpriest <benjamin.m.priest@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 03:09:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] net: keep a --lan-join guest trying until its host
 answers


start_client blocks for up to five seconds and a failed --lan-join was
final, so a guest whose launcher started it before the host's emulator was
listening never joined. Netplay.pak starts both devices independently, so
that ordering is common.

Split the join into begin_join/step_join. The frontend waits up to two
seconds for a host that is already up, then keeps the attempt running from
the frame loop (step_join(0), restarted every second after a failure) and
goes live the moment the host answers, without freezing the game.
start_client keeps its old blocking behaviour on top of the same code.
---
 src/frontend/sdl/main.cpp | 57 ++++++++++++++++++++------
 src/net/lan_mp.cpp        | 84 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 src/net/lan_mp.h          | 11 +++++
 3 files changed, 112 insertions(+), 40 deletions(-)

